<LessonLayout
  step={2}
  heading="B. Believe that only Jesus Christ can save."
  description="Salvation is not by works but by grace through faith in Jesus Christ alone."
>
  <p>
    We have seen that <strong>all have sinned</strong> and that the wages of
    sin is death. But God has provided a way for us to be saved.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Romans 6:23b</strong>
  </p>

  <p>
    "But the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord."
  </p>

  <p>
    Eternal life is God's gift, and that gift is found in
    <strong>Jesus Christ</strong>.
  </p>

  <p>
    We cannot save ourselves from sin by trying to become a better person.
    Our good deeds cannot erase our sins, and our religious works cannot
    make us righteous before God.
  </p>

  <p>
    Salvation is not something we earn. It is something God freely gives
    through Jesus Christ when we place our faith in Him.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Titus 3:5</strong>
  </p>

  <p>
    "Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to
    his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of
    the Holy Ghost;"
  </p>

  <p>
    Notice what the Bible says: <strong
      >"Not by works of righteousness which we have done."</strong
    >
  </p>

  <p>
    We cannot earn salvation by doing good works. We cannot earn it by
    being religious, helping others, giving money, attending church, or
    trying to live a good life.
  </p>

  <p>
    If salvation could be earned by our own works, we could take credit
    for it. But salvation is entirely according to God's mercy and grace.
  </p>

  <p>
    The answer to our sin problem is not found in what <strong>we</strong>
    can do for God, but in what <strong
      >Jesus Christ has already done for us</strong
    >.
  </p>

  <!-- Update 10-26-26: removed a stray verse number "9" inside the quote below -->
  <p>
    <strong>Ephesians 2:8-9</strong>
  </p>

  <p>
    "For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves:
    it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast."
  </p>

  <p>
    The Bible teaches that we are saved <strong
      >by grace through faith</strong
    >. Salvation is God's gift. It is not something we can earn through
    good works.
  </p>

  <p>
    We must put our faith in <strong>Jesus Christ</strong>—trusting Him as
    the only One who can save us from our sins.
  </p>

  <p>
    Good works are important, but they are not the way we receive
    salvation. We do not do good works <em>in order to be saved</em>;
    rather, good works should follow as the fruit of a life that has been
    changed by God.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Jesus Christ is the answer to our sin problem.</strong>
  </p>

  <p>
    You cannot save yourself. You cannot work your way into heaven.
    Salvation is by God's grace, through faith in Jesus Christ alone.
  </p>

  <p>
    The question now is: <strong
      >How can you receive this gift of salvation?</strong
    >
  </p>
</LessonLayout>
